      ":question/problem": "$\\displaystyle\\int \\left(y^{2}-4\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y=$\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(y^{2}-4\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y &= \\int \\left(y^{2}-4\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &= \\int y^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}y-4\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ &= \\frac{y^{2+1}}{(2+1)}-4\\frac{y^{0+1}}{(0+1)}+C \\\\ &= \\frac{y^{3}}{3}-4y+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
